  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-11-14T04:54:10.613Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Within VRChat at the moment, users can Show/Hide specific users avatars if they wish. However, an option to set your own Avatar's visibility would be quite beneficial.\n\nWhat this means is Person A could set there avatar visibility to \"Hidden\", and Person B who shows Persons A avatar will not be able to see there avatar, because Person A has set it to hidden.\n\nIdeally, this could be set on a case by case basis, so if I don't want a specific person (or even a specific rank) to see my avatar, I could set it.\n\nThis could potentially help with issues relating to Avatar Theft by gatekeeping who can see your avatar. The only issue for this would be potential issues with moderation, which will need to be addressed if this suggestion is taken to heart.",
